Concurrency concern with H2: two threads insert same PK. H2 MVStore: second blocks until first commits, then DuplicateKeyException. Then we read row — but our read is outside tx; row committed → visible. If first rolled back, row gone → retry insert (bounded attempts). If row present but body null (first still in progress — can't happen if insert blocked... unless H2 threw immediately). Handle with short wait-retry loop (up to ~5s), then 409 "请求处理中，请重试"? Actually spec: same key same params → return first result. Under concurrency, returning "in progress" 409 would fail the concurrency test expectation if it occurs. With blocking insert, after first commits, second's insert throws dup key and row is complete. So body-null case is unlikely; still handle with retry loop for robustness.

Timeout/retry: loop attempts with 50ms sleep, max 100 attempts (5s). Then throw ApiException 409.

