H2 MySQL mode: table-level `COMMENT='...'` — H2 supports `COMMENT 'text'` after table definition? H2 supports `COMMENT` on table via `COMMENT ON TABLE`. Inline table comment in MySQL mode... H2 2.x in MySQL compatibility mode supports `COMMENT 'string'` at table level? I think H2 supports it. If not, schema init fails and I'll see it in build/test. Column COMMENT is supported by H2 (it's H2's own syntax too). Table COMMENT inline — H2 docs: "COMMENT" is supported in CREATE TABLE for columns; for table comment, MySQL-style `COMMENT='x'`... H2 MySQL mode does support `COMMENT` table option I believe. To reduce risk, skip table-level comments, keep column comments only. Column COMMENT is definitely supported in H2 (standard H2 grammar: `columnName type [COMMENT 'string']`).

TIMESTAMP in H2 = timestamp without time zone. Storing Instants via JdbcTemplate: use `Timestamp.from(instant)` and read via `rs.getTimestamp(...).toInstant()`. Values interpreted in JVM default TZ — consistent within JVM. Fine.

